# Keeps the production image lean and — more importantly — keeps real secrets out of
# image layers. Without this, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile bakes .env (real DB/CRM/session
# secrets), .git (652K, full history), and .venv (107M, redundant — pip installs its own
# site-packages inside the image) straight into the image. Runtime config now reaches the
# container via docker-compose's `env_file: .env` instead (see docker-compose.yml).

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

.git/
.gitignore
.github/

.env
.env.*
!.env.example

.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Dev-only docs and test suite — not needed at runtime, only bloat the image.
tests/
README.md
project_plan.md
